{"name":"Old Porch","hex":"#745947","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"old","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mochi."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an object, concept, relationship, etc., having existed for a relatively long period of time.","Of a living being, having lived for most of the expected years."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old"},{"term":"porch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A covered entrance to a building, whether taken from the interior, and forming a sort of vestibule within the main wall, or projecting without and with a separate roof. A porch often has chair(s), table(s) and swings.","A portico; a covered walk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Porch","blocks":[{"text":"A porch is a room or gallery located in front of an entrance to a building. A porch is placed in front of the façade of a building it commands, and forms a low front. Alternatively, it may be a vestibule or a projecting building that houses the entrance door of a building."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Chartres_Cathedral_020_south_facade_TTaylor.JPG/330px-Chartres_Cathedral_020_south_facade_TTaylor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porch","wikidata":"Q816741"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/London_-_Cromwell_Road_-_Natural_History_Museum_1881_by_Alfred_Waterhouse_-_View_NW_%26_Up_at_the_Entrance_on_the_Terracotta_Tiled_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg/500px-London_-_Cromwell_Road_-_Natural_History_Museum_1881_by_Alfred_Waterhouse_-_View_NW_%26_Up_at_the_Entrance_on_the_Terracotta_Tiled_Fa%C3%A7ade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/London_-_Cromwell_Road_-_Natural_History_Museum_1881_by